{"v":1,"n":2,"of":2,"html":"<div style=\"display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:8px;margin:0;padding:0\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"position:relative;flex:0 0 108px;width:108px;min-height:36px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:10px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#C79A12;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:31px;top:0;bottom:0;width:6px;background:#173D31;opacity:0.3;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:50px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#00875A;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:70px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#A56E17;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:27px;top:4px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#FFFFFF;border:3px solid #173D31;z-index:5\"></span></div><details style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;margin:0 0 12px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font:14px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;color:#141B22;padding:2px 0 0;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden\"><strong style=\"font-weight:800\">Nov–Dec 1988</strong> · Eviction, demolition</summary><div style=\"display:block;position:relative;z-index:5;margin:6px 0 4px;padding:10px 12px;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #C9CED3;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.12);font:14px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;color:#1E252B\"><div style=\"font:700 14px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;margin:0 0 4px\">Nov–Dec 1988 · Eviction, then demolition (6 Dec 1988)</div><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:0 4px 4px 0;border-radius:9px;background:#E3F2E7;color:#0B5D2A;border:1px solid #9CCBAA;vertical-align:1px\">VERIFIED · press</span></div>Possession was enforced at the end of November 1988 (forced entry reported for 30 Nov). The farmhouse was demolished in early December 1988: 6 December in this entry’s sources (<a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0108-south-wales-echo-bp-demolition-anger/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0108</a>), reported on 7 December (<a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0106-tears-flow-farmhouse-razed-1988/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0106</a>). The exact day is an open question.<br /><span style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#444\">Source: <a href=\"/wiki/demolition-1988/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">1988 demolition</a> · <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0108-south-wales-echo-bp-demolition-anger/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0108</a></span></div></details></div><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:8px;margin:0;padding:0\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"position:relative;flex:0 0 108px;width:108px;min-height:36px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:10px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#C79A12;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:31px;top:0;bottom:0;width:6px;background:#173D31;opacity:0.3;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:50px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#00875A;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:70px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#A56E17;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:7px;top:4px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#FFFFFF;border:3px solid #0E7C86;z-index:5\"></span></div><details style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;margin:0 0 12px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font:14px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;color:#141B22;padding:2px 0 0;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden\"><strong style=\"font-weight:800\">1989–90</strong> · Outline planning</summary><div style=\"display:block;position:relative;z-index:5;margin:6px 0 4px;padding:10px 12px;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #C9CED3;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.12);font:14px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;color:#1E252B\"><div style=\"font:700 14px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;margin:0 0 4px\">1989–90 · Planning 89/01396/OUT: Cardiff Bay Development Corporation consulted</div><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:0 4px 4px 0;border-radius:9px;background:#E3F2E7;color:#0B5D2A;border:1px solid #9CCBAA;vertical-align:1px\">VERIFIED · scan read</span></div>BP Properties’ outline application (received 8 Nov 1989; granted 13 Mar 1990). The planning officer’s report lists among the consultees: <em>“Cardiff Bay Development Corporation: No objections – however, the Corporation would hope that the trees on the slope of the site facing north-west are retained and that the public right of way which runs through the site will be retained.”</em> This is Cardiff Bay Development Corporation, not Cardiff City Council. The full response is outstanding; it was requested from the Vale on 18 Sep 2026.<br /><span style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#444\">Source: <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0201-planning-officer-s-report-on-outline-application-f/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0201 (report scan, p.1)</a> · <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0124-outline-planning-permission-89-01396-out-residenti/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0124</a> · <a href=\"/wiki/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/vale-of-glamorgan-council-email-correspondence-catalogue/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">request to the Vale</a></span></div></details></div><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:8px;margin:0;padding:0\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"position:relative;flex:0 0 108px;width:108px;min-height:36px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:10px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#C79A12;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:31px;top:0;bottom:0;width:6px;background:#173D31;opacity:0.3;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:50px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#00875A;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:70px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#A56E17;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:7px;top:4px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#FFFFFF;border:3px solid #C79A12;z-index:5\"></span></div><details style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;margin:0 0 12px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font:14px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;color:#141B22;padding:2px 0 0;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden\"><strong style=\"font-weight:800\">1992</strong> · Reserved matters</summary><div style=\"display:block;position:relative;z-index:5;margin:6px 0 4px;padding:10px 12px;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #C9CED3;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.12);font:14px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;color:#1E252B\"><div style=\"font:700 14px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;margin:0 0 4px\">1992 · Reserved matters 92/00671/RES: 20 houses; no Cardiff body named</div><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:0 4px 4px 0;border-radius:9px;background:#E3F2E7;color:#0B5D2A;border:1px solid #9CCBAA;vertical-align:1px\">VERIFIED · scan read</span></div>Ideal Homes Wales’ Form D (14 May 1992) names no Cardiff City or Cardiff Bay body. It answers “No” to felling trees and “No” to altering or diverting a public right of way. The <a class=\"cw-n\" href=\"/nomenclature/c/heneb/\" data-n=\"heneb\" data-tip=\"Heneb (formerly GGAT) — The Welsh archaeological trust that holds the Historic Environment Record for the area.\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\">GGAT</a> letter of 27 Jul 1992 (EV-0128) is not published here.<br /><span style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#444\">Source: <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0127-planning-application-form-d-for-approval-of-reserv/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0127 (form scan)</a> · <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0128-ggat-letter-reserved-matters-approval/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0128</a></span></div></details></div><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:8px;margin:0;padding:0\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"position:relative;flex:0 0 108px;width:108px;min-height:36px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:10px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#C79A12;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:31px;top:0;bottom:0;width:6px;background:#173D31;opacity:0.3;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:50px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#00875A;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:70px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#A56E17;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:7px;top:4px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#FFFFFF;border:3px solid #C79A12;z-index:5\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:47px;top:4px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#FFFFFF;border:3px solid #00875A;z-index:5\"></span></div><details style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;margin:0 0 12px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font:14px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;color:#141B22;padding:2px 0 0;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden\"><strong style=\"font-weight:800\">3 Dec 1993</strong> · BP → Ideal Homes</summary><div style=\"display:block;position:relative;z-index:5;margin:6px 0 4px;padding:10px 12px;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #C9CED3;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.12);font:14px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;color:#1E252B\"><div style=\"font:700 14px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;margin:0 0 4px\">3 Dec 1993 · BP → Ideal Homes (farm site and woodland)</div><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:0 4px 4px 0;border-radius:9px;background:#ECEFF1;color:#37474F;border:1px solid #B0BEC5;vertical-align:1px\">REPORTED</span></div>Recorded in the woodland title history on the wiki; the houses became Church View Close. Forest of Cardiff states that it bought the woodland from Ideal Homes (now Persimmon) “after due diligence”. Deed not seen.<br /><span style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#444\">Source: <a href=\"/wiki/scrutiny-and-accountability/government-public-authority-involvement/forest-of-cardiff-forensic-institutional-review/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">Forest of Cardiff review</a></span></div></details></div><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:8px;margin:0;padding:0\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"position:relative;flex:0 0 108px;width:108px;min-height:36px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:10px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#C79A12;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:31px;top:0;bottom:0;width:6px;background:#173D31;opacity:0.3;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:50px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#00875A;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:70px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#A56E17;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:47px;top:4px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#FFFFFF;border:3px solid #00875A;z-index:5\"></span></div><details style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;margin:0 0 12px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font:14px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;color:#141B22;padding:2px 0 0;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden\"><strong style=\"font-weight:800\">10 Nov 1994</strong> · Change of hands</summary><div style=\"display:block;position:relative;z-index:5;margin:6px 0 4px;padding:10px 12px;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #C9CED3;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.12);font:14px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;color:#1E252B\"><div style=\"font:700 14px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;margin:0 0 4px\">10 Nov 1994 · Woodland transferred to Forest of Cardiff, title WA735527; a separate event from the 1961 deed</div><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:0 4px 4px 0;border-radius:9px;background:#E3F2E7;color:#0B5D2A;border:1px solid #9CCBAA;vertical-align:1px\">RECORD · register read · grade 2 (transfer not read)</span></div>Transfer with plan to Forest of Cardiff, registered as WA735527. The current register (EV-0169) was read; the 1994 transfer itself (EV-0136) is not published here. Forest of Cardiff’s accounts to 31 Mar 1995 show no land as an asset. The register (B1) enters Forest of Cardiff as proprietor on 25 Nov 1994. It recites a 23 May 1975 conveyance of part (“the land tinted blue … and other land”) from The British Petroleum Pension Trust to B.P. Properties Ltd, and notes copies of earlier deeds as “filed under WA231076”. It is a separate event from the 1961 deed.<br /><span style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#444\">Source: <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0169-wa735527-title-register-september-2026/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0169</a> · <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0136-forest-of-cardiff-woodland-transfer-1994/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0136</a></span></div></details></div><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:8px;margin:0;padding:0\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"position:relative;flex:0 0 108px;width:108px;min-height:26px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:10px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#C79A12;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:31px;top:0;bottom:0;width:6px;background:#173D31;opacity:0.3;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:50px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#00875A;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:70px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#A56E17;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:48px;top:5px;width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:2px;transform:rotate(45deg);background:#00875A;z-index:5\"></span></div><div style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;margin:0 0 10px;padding:0\"><span style=\"display:inline;font:700 11px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.03em;padding:2px 7px;border-radius:4px;background:#E8F5EF;color:#00603F;border-left:4px solid #00875A\">WOODLAND · change of hands / new proprietor</span><span style=\"font:12px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;color:#4A535C\"> (or, on the family’s reading, further parcel creation) · not the 1961 deed</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:8px;margin:0;padding:0\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"position:relative;flex:0 0 108px;width:108px;min-height:36px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:10px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#C79A12;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:31px;top:0;bottom:0;width:6px;background:#173D31;opacity:0.3;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:50px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#00875A;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:70px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#A56E17;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:47px;top:4px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#FFFFFF;border:3px solid #00875A;z-index:5\"></span></div><details style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;margin:0 0 12px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font:14px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;color:#141B22;padding:2px 0 0;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden\"><strong style=\"font-weight:800\">2005–06</strong> · WA735527 part sold</summary><div style=\"display:block;position:relative;z-index:5;margin:6px 0 4px;padding:10px 12px;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #C9CED3;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.12);font:14px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;color:#1E252B\"><div style=\"font:700 14px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;margin:0 0 4px\">2005–06 · Part of WA735527 sold to Goldsworthy Homes: £20,000</div><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:0 4px 4px 0;border-radius:9px;background:#E3F2E7;color:#0B5D2A;border:1px solid #9CCBAA;vertical-align:1px\">RECORD · accounts + register · grade 1</span></div>A 2005 transfer excised land from WA735527 (EV-0139); register entry A4 dated 22 Dec 2005 records the excised land being registered under a new title. Forest of Cardiff’s audited accounts to 30 Jun 2006 record “Sale of Land – Leckwith Road, Llandough £20,000”.<br /><span style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#444\">Source: <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0217-forest-of-cardiff-accounts-2006-sale-of-land-leckwith-road/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0217</a> · <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0139-forest-cardiff-goldsworthy-transfer-excision/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0139</a></span></div></details></div><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:8px;margin:0;padding:0\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"position:relative;flex:0 0 108px;width:108px;min-height:26px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:10px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#C79A12;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:31px;top:0;bottom:0;width:6px;background:#173D31;opacity:0.3;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:50px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#00875A;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:70px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#A56E17;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:48px;top:5px;width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:2px;transform:rotate(45deg);background:#00875A;z-index:5\"></span></div><div style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;margin:0 0 10px;padding:0\"><span style=\"display:inline;font:700 11px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.03em;padding:2px 7px;border-radius:4px;background:#E8F5EF;color:#00603F;border-left:4px solid #00875A\">WOODLAND · change of hands / new proprietor</span><span style=\"font:12px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;color:#4A535C\"> (or, on the family’s reading, further parcel creation)</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:8px;margin:0;padding:0\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"position:relative;flex:0 0 108px;width:108px;min-height:36px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:10px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#C79A12;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:31px;top:0;bottom:0;width:6px;background:#173D31;opacity:0.3;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:50px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#00875A;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:70px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:#A56E17;z-index:1\"></span></div><div style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0\"><details style=\"margin:0 0 10px;border:1px solid #C9CED3;border-radius:6px;background:#F7F8F9\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;padding:8px 10px;font:700 13px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;color:#2B333B;white-space:normal\">Interval table: every candidate interval, line by line</summary><div style=\"padding:0 10px 10px;position:relative;z-index:5;background:#F7F8F9\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:8px;margin:0;padding:0\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0\"><div style=\"margin:2px 0 14px;padding:10px 10px 4px;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #D5DADF;border-left:5px solid #5B2C83;border-radius:6px\"><div style=\"font:800 14px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;color:#141B22\">Each line’s interval, to scale. These compare different event types (a surrender and re-grant, a tenancy offer, licence letters; a deed, a green registration, a <a class=\"cw-g\" href=\"/glossary/#first-registration\" data-tip=\"First registration: Registering a piece of land with HM Land Registry for the first time, usually after a sale or transfer. The deeds before it are not copied onto the register.\">first registration</a>) under different legal rules; they are not a measured pattern. A green registration rests on 20 years’ use as of right, not 12 years’ possession.</div><div style=\"font:12.5px/1.45 Arial,sans-serif;color:#4A535C;margin:2px 0 8px\">Coloured bar = the earlier event → the later registration, on each line. Purple bracket = 12 years from the attempt (the limitation period for adverse possession of unregistered land, Limitation Act 1980 s.15; 1939 Act before it). Real gaps shown, not rounded to 12.</div><div style=\"position:relative;height:14px;margin:0 0 6px;font:11px/1 Arial,sans-serif;color:#5B6670\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:calc(11.11% - 12px)\">1950</span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:calc(33.33% - 12px)\">1960</span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:calc(55.56% - 12px)\">1970</span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:calc(77.78% - 12px)\">1980</span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:calc(100.0% - 24px)\">1990</span></div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px\"><div style=\"font:800 13px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;color:#00875A\">Line 1 · Woodland</div><div style=\"position:relative;height:30px;margin:3px 0 2px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:11.11%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:33.33%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:55.56%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:77.78%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:100.0%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:8.89%;width:26.67%;top:3px;height:7px;border:2px solid #5B2C83;border-bottom:none\" title=\"12-year waiting period\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:8.89%;width:27.2%;top:15px;height:9px;background:#00875A;border-radius:2px\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:calc(8.89% - 6px);top:13px;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:#fff;border:3px solid #00875A\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:calc(36.09% - 6px);top:13px;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:#00875A;border:3px solid #00875A\"></span></div><div style=\"font:12.5px/1.45 Arial,sans-serif;color:#1E252B\"><strong>1949 attempt</strong> → <strong>1961 deed</strong>: <strong>about 12 years</strong>. 1949: the surrender and re-grant of 2 Feb 1949 (1987 judgment); 1961: the 29 Mar 1961 deed recited on WA735527. <span style=\"color:#444\">Source: <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0040-1961-wgr-brick-tile-deed/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0040</a> · <a href=\"/wayback/go/?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bailii.org%2Few%2Fcases%2FEWCA%2FCiv%2F1987%2F2.html\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">1987 judgment</a></span></div></div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px\"><div style=\"font:800 13px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;color:#A56E17\">Line 2 · Green (VG41)</div><div style=\"position:relative;height:30px;margin:3px 0 2px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:11.11%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:33.33%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:55.56%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:77.78%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:100.0%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:30.0%;width:26.67%;top:3px;height:7px;border:2px solid #5B2C83;border-bottom:none\" title=\"12-year waiting period\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:30.0%;width:26.58%;top:15px;height:9px;background:#A56E17;border-radius:2px\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:calc(30.0% - 6px);top:13px;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:#fff;border:3px solid #A56E17\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:calc(56.58% - 6px);top:13px;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:#A56E17;border:3px solid #A56E17\"></span></div><div style=\"font:12.5px/1.45 Arial,sans-serif;color:#1E252B\"><strong>1958/9 attempt</strong> → <strong>16 Jun 1970 registration VG41</strong>: <strong>about 11–12 years</strong> (12 from 1958, 11 from 1959). <span style=\"color:#444\">Source: <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0039-wgr-tenancy-offers-1959-1965/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0039</a> · <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0044-vg41-village-green-registration-1970/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0044</a></span></div></div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px\"><div style=\"font:800 13px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;color:#C8102E\">Line 3 · BP house (WA240304)</div><div style=\"position:relative;height:30px;margin:3px 0 2px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:11.11%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:33.33%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:55.56%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:77.78%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:100.0%;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:#D3D8DD\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:66.29%;width:26.669999999999987%;top:3px;height:7px;border:2px solid #5B2C83;border-bottom:none\" title=\"12-year waiting period\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:66.29%;width:18.49%;top:15px;height:9px;background:#C8102E;border-radius:2px\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:calc(55.53% - 4px);top:15px;width:5px;height:5px;border-radius:50%;background:#fff;border:2px solid #C8102E\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:calc(58.89% - 4px);top:15px;width:5px;height:5px;border-radius:50%;background:#fff;border:2px solid #C8102E\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:calc(66.29% - 6px);top:13px;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:#fff;border:3px solid #C8102E\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:calc(84.78% - 6px);top:13px;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:#C8102E;border:3px solid #C8102E\"></span></div><div style=\"font:12.5px/1.45 Arial,sans-serif;color:#1E252B\"><strong>31 Oct 1974 letters</strong> → <strong>23 Feb 1983 registration</strong>: <strong>8 years 4 months</strong>. Small dots: from the 31 Dec 1969 acquisition, 13 years 2 months; from 1971, about 12 years. <span style=\"color:#444\">Source: <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0050-1974-bp-licence-letters/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0050</a> · <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0066-hmlr-wa240304-item-10-register-1983/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0066</a> · <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0043-wgr-bp-pension-trust-conveyance/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0043</a></span></div></div><div style=\"font:12.5px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;color:#1E252B;margin:4px 0 6px\">On each line the registration came about 12 years after the rejected attempt. <span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:0 4px 4px 0;border-radius:9px;background:#FFF1CC;color:#6B4300;border:1px solid #E5C066;vertical-align:1px\">SOURCE PENDING</span> Whether Mary or the registry was told, until the full registry files are seen.</div></div></div></div></div></details></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:8px;margin:0;padding:0\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"position:relative;flex:0 0 108px;width:108px;min-height:36px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:10px;top:0;height:11px;width:8px;background:#C79A12;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:31px;top:0;bottom:0;width:6px;background:#173D31;opacity:0.3;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:50px;top:0;height:11px;width:8px;background:#00875A;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:70px;top:0;height:11px;width:8px;background:#A56E17;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:7px;top:4px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#FFFFFF;border:3px solid #C79A12;z-index:5\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:47px;top:4px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#FFFFFF;border:3px solid #00875A;z-index:5\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:67px;top:4px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#FFFFFF;border:3px solid #A56E17;z-index:5\"></span></div><details style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;margin:0 0 12px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font:14px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;color:#141B22;padding:2px 0 0;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden\"><strong style=\"font-weight:800\">2026</strong> · Where each line stands</summary><div style=\"display:block;position:relative;z-index:5;margin:6px 0 4px;padding:10px 12px;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #C9CED3;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.12);font:14px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;color:#1E252B\"><div style=\"font:700 14px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;margin:0 0 4px\">2026 · Where each title stands today</div><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:0 4px 4px 0;border-radius:9px;background:#E3F2E7;color:#0B5D2A;border:1px solid #9CCBAA;vertical-align:1px\">RECORD · registers read · grade 2</span></div><strong>Merged title WA231076</strong> (house third + Parcel B): built over as Church View Close. <strong>Forest third:</strong> Forest of Cardiff, WA735527. <strong>Green third:</strong> village green VG41. <strong>Provisional Parcel A:</strong> no register shows a Williams title; present legal status unresolved. HM Land Registry copies of the 1982–83 files are on order.<br /><span style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#444\">Source: <a href=\"/wiki/land-registry-titles/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">Land Registry titles</a> · <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0169-wa735527-title-register-september-2026/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0169</a> · <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0044-vg41-village-green-registration-1970/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0044</a></span></div></details></div><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:8px;margin:0;padding:0\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"position:relative;flex:0 0 108px;width:108px;min-height:36px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:31px;top:0;bottom:0;width:6px;background:#173D31;opacity:0.3;z-index:1\"></span><span style=\"position:absolute;left:27px;top:4px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#FFFFFF;border:3px solid #173D31;z-index:5\"></span></div><details style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;margin:0 0 12px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font:14px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;color:#141B22;padding:2px 0 0;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden\"><strong style=\"font-weight:800\">2026</strong> · Provisional Parcel A: status unresolved</summary><div style=\"display:block;position:relative;z-index:5;margin:6px 0 4px;padding:10px 12px;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #C9CED3;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.12);font:14px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;color:#1E252B\"><div style=\"font:700 14px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;margin:0 0 4px\">2026 · Provisional Parcel A: no Williams conveyance identified in the reviewed public file; present legal status unresolved</div><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:0 4px 4px 0;border-radius:9px;background:#E3F2E7;color:#0B5D2A;border:1px solid #9CCBAA;vertical-align:1px\">OPEN QUESTION · registers + judgment</span></div>No deed of sale by Mary (Nancy) Williams is on file, and the 1987 appeal decided the farmhouse and garden only. No register read so far shows a Williams title to the provisional Parcel A; a register cannot prove a negative. <span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:0 4px 4px 0;border-radius:9px;background:#FFF1CC;color:#6B4300;border:1px solid #E5C066;vertical-align:1px\">SOURCE PENDING</span> A sale c.1965 reported in a cousin’s written account (held privately) is unidentified.<br /><span style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#444\">Source: <a href=\"/wiki/claim-parcel-a-parcel-b-distinct-histories-1987-amalgamation\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">Parcel A / B claim</a> · <a href=\"/wiki/the-two-parcels/three-parts-of-parcel-a-divergent-chronologies/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">Three Parts of Parcel A</a></span></div></details></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:8px\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"position:relative;flex:0 0 108px;width:108px;height:46px\"><span style=\"position:absolute;left:31px;top:0;bottom:0;width:6px;background:#173D31;opacity:0.3;z-index:1\"></span></div><div style=\"flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;font:italic 12.5px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;color:#5B6670;padding-top:6px\">Provisional Parcel A: present legal status unresolved.</div></div><details style=\"margin:0 0 10px;border:1px solid #C9CED3;border-radius:6px;background:#F7F8F9\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;padding:8px 10px;font:700 13px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;color:#2B333B;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden\">What cuts against this reading</summary><div style=\"padding:0 10px 10px;position:relative;z-index:5;background:#F7F8F9\"><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font:12.5px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;color:#4A3B2A\"><strong>What cuts against this reading:</strong> the Court of Appeal records that the possessory-title claim to the rest of the farm failed on the facts and was not appealed, and it held that the 1974 letters made the house occupancy a licence. No record yet links the three registrations to each other. <a href=\"/wayback/go/?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bailii.org%2Few%2Fcases%2FEWCA%2FCiv%2F1987%2F2.html\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">1987 judgment</a></p></div></details><div style=\"height:12px\"></div><details style=\"margin:0 0 10px;border:1px solid #C9CED3;border-radius:6px;background:#F7F8F9\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;padding:8px 10px;font:700 13px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;color:#2B333B;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden\">A wider plan?</summary><div style=\"padding:0 10px 10px;position:relative;z-index:5;background:#F7F8F9\"><section style=\"margin:0 0 16px;padding:12px 12px 8px;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #D5DADF;border-top:5px solid #7B3FB0;border-radius:6px\"><h3 style=\"margin:0 0 2px;font:800 16px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;color:#141B22;letter-spacing:.01em\">A wider plan?</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font:13px/1.45 Arial,sans-serif;color:#4A535C\">Shown as a question.</p><div style=\"padding:8px 10px;background:#FBF7FF;border:1px dashed #B990DE;border-radius:6px;font:13.5px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;color:#2E1A40\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:2px 0 0 4px;border-radius:9px;background:#F3E8FD;color:#5B2C83;border:1px solid #CDB0E8;vertical-align:1px\">QUESTION</span> Was there a wider plan for the land on which the Williams family were not consulted? This is not established. Records that bear on it:<ul style=\"margin:6px 0 4px;padding:0 0 0 18px\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 3px\">Oct–Nov 1988: BP’s pension fund sells about 1,300 acres of Welsh land to Intercontinental Land &amp; Development (Cardiff) Ltd; the Land Authority for Wales buys sites from Lavernock to Leckwith <span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:2px 0 0 4px;border-radius:9px;background:#ECEFF1;color:#37474F;border:1px solid #B0BEC5;vertical-align:1px\">REPORTED · press snippets</span></li><li style=\"margin:0 0 3px\">21 Oct–25 Nov 1988: Land Authority for Wales board papers (TNA WA 9/49), open at Kew <span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:2px 0 0 4px;border-radius:9px;background:#ECEFF1;color:#37474F;border:1px solid #B0BEC5;vertical-align:1px\">REPORTED · catalogue only, not read</span></li><li style=\"margin:0 0 3px\">9 Nov 1989: Land Authority advertises building land at Lewis Road, about 270 m from the farmhouse, the same week 89/01396/OUT went in <span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:2px 0 0 4px;border-radius:9px;background:#ECEFF1;color:#37474F;border:1px solid #B0BEC5;vertical-align:1px\">REPORTED · press snippet</span></li><li style=\"margin:0 0 3px\">1989: Cardiff Bay Development Corporation consulted on 89/01396/OUT <span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:2px 0 0 4px;border-radius:9px;background:#E3F2E7;color:#0B5D2A;border:1px solid #9CCBAA;vertical-align:1px\">VERIFIED</span> <a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0201-planning-officer-s-report-on-outline-application-f/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0201</a></li><li style=\"margin:0 0 3px\">Nov 1994: Land Authority gives 127 acres between Leckwith Hill and <a class=\"cw-n\" href=\"/nomenclature/c/llandough/\" data-n=\"llandough\" data-tip=\"Llandough (near Penarth) — The parish and village beside Penarth and Cardiff where the farm stood.\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\">Llandough</a> to the county council <span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:2px 0 0 4px;border-radius:9px;background:#ECEFF1;color:#37474F;border:1px solid #B0BEC5;vertical-align:1px\">REPORTED · press snippet</span></li></ul><strong>Cuts against:</strong> on every record seen so far, the farm itself stayed with BP until its 1993 sale to Ideal Homes. The 1988 buyer was a private company after a tender, and the Land Authority held neighbouring land, not <a class=\"cw-n\" href=\"/nomenclature/c/great-house-farm/\" data-n=\"tymawr\" data-tip=\"Great House Farm — The English farm name, in Glamorgan Archives D/D XJF 64/30 and in the Historic Environment Record (GGAT02038s).\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\">Great House Farm</a>. <strong>What would settle it:</strong> the Land Authority board papers (WA 9/49), the full Cardiff Bay Development Corporation response, and the <a class=\"cw-g\" href=\"/glossary/#village-green\" data-tip=\"Village green (VG41): Land registered as a town or village green. VG41 is the green at Church View Close, Llandough.\">VG41</a> file.</div></section></div></details><details style=\"margin:0 0 10px;border:1px solid #C9CED3;border-radius:6px;background:#F7F8F9\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;padding:8px 10px;font:700 13px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;color:#2B333B;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden\">Reading rule and notes</summary><div style=\"padding:0 10px 10px;position:relative;z-index:5;background:#F7F8F9\"><div style=\"margin:12px 0 0;padding:8px 0 0;border-top:1px solid #C6CBD0;font:12px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;color:#4D555E\"><strong>Reading rule:</strong> the decisive test is each deed, order and registration plan laid over the same three Parcel-A areas. Local history only, not title events: Marconi’s wireless trials at Lavernock, May 1897 (<a href=\"/wiki/evidence/ev-0011-marconi-lavernock-wireless-cutting-1897/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">EV-0011</a>); Peerless Jim Driscoll’s first fight in the barn <span style=\"display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;font:700 10px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;margin:2px 0 0 4px;border-radius:9px;background:#ECEFF1;color:#37474F;border:1px solid #B0BEC5;vertical-align:1px\">REPORTED · date unknown</span>. Map rebuilt 19 Oct 2026; the previous version is kept in the template’s revision history. <a href=\"/wiki/master-change-log-october-2026/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">Change log</a> · <a href=\"/wiki/the-two-parcels/three-parts-of-parcel-a-divergent-chronologies/\" style=\"color:#0B57A4;text-decoration:underline\">Three Parts of Parcel A</a></div></div></details>"}